{"files_reviewed":["apps/kaipu-record/src/shared/types/workspaces.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.test.ts"],"files_skipped":[],"findings":[{"path":"apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx","line":168,"severity":"consider","topic":"tests","confidence":"high","title":"No test checks that an unchanged relocate shows no toast","body":"The new flag is asserted only at the start of its path, in `relocate.test.ts:158`. Nothing checks the two steps that make the fix visible to the user:
- `relocateFolder` copying `unchanged` into the IPC result (`index.ts:349`);
- `onRelocated` returning before `showToast`.

The Settings tests only check the case where the toast does appear (`workspaces-settings.test.tsx:262` and `:282`). If either step stopped passing the flag along, the "now points to the new folder" toast would come back and no test would fail.

Suggested test: in `workspaces-settings.test.tsx`, mock `relocate` to resolve `{ ok: true, workspace, unchanged: true }` and assert that `showToast` is not called."}],"contracts":[{"action":"Picking the folder the workspace already points at in "Change folder…" returns `unchanged: true`, and the renderer then skips the "now points" toast","location":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:43","equivalent_path":"A real relocate: `registry.relocate`, or `relocateActive` for the active workspace, then `relocateFolder` runs the probe, refreshes titles, broadcasts and returns the view","before_after":"`checkRelocate` and `relocateRefusal` still run before the early return. `relocateFolder` still runs `availability` (which rewrites an identity deleted by hand), `refreshTitles` and `broadcastState`, the same as a real relocate. The only difference is the flag in the result.","visible_effect":"`onRelocated` in the context returns early, so neither the dialog nor Settings shows a toast. The dialog stays open, as it does after a real relocate.","failure_mode":"The failure path is unchanged: when the IPC call rejects, the context shows `relocateUncertain`. A refusal still reaches `relocateRefusalMessage`.","status":"closed","evidence":["apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/relocate.ts:33-48","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts:340-350","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspaces-context.tsx:165-192","apps/kaipu-record/src/renderer/src/features/workspaces/workspace-dialog.tsx:145","apps/kaipu-record/src/shared/types/workspaces.ts:163-169"],"open_question":"","candidates":[]},{"action":"An offline edit of a `pendingInit` workspace keeps `pendingInit` set when the folder was not written","location":"apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:634","equivalent_path":"The `availability` probe clears `pendingInit` only after it writes or finds an identity, and `add` clears it only when it relocates","before_after":"When the folder comes back, the no-identity branch of the probe writes `identity.json` with the edited name and color, then clears `pendingInit` and `pendingIdentity`. `checkRelocate` keeps accepting a moved folder that has Kaipu items and no identity while `pendingInit` is set.","visible_effect":""Change folder…" on that workspace now accepts the remounted folder instead of refusing it as `has-items-no-identity`.","failure_mode":"If the registry write fails, `update` rolls back and `edit` returns `not-writable`. Nothing was written to the folder in this branch, so there is nothing to undo.","status":"closed","evidence":["apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:603-650","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:731-754","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry.ts:847-856","apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/registry-relocate.test.ts:221-243"],"open_question":"","candidates":[]}],"thread_replies":[{"comment_id":4438597053,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the fix in 886d67f0 as described."},{"comment_id":4438597058,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed: the rollback now calls `removeIdentity` when `previous.kind === "absent"` (registry.ts:645-646)."},{"comment_id":4438597062,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's diff. Accepting the separate name and color checks from 886d67f0."},{"comment_id":4438597064,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed: `edit` re-runs `validateWorkspaceName` inside the locked `update` and reports `name-taken` (registry.ts:626, 648)."},{"comment_id":4438597067,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the edit-specific messages from 886d67f0."},{"comment_id":4438597070,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the `act`-wrapped late answer from 886d67f0."},{"comment_id":4438597073,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the updated ADR status row."},{"comment_id":4439290166,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed: `checkRelocate` accepts a folder with items and no identity for a `pendingInit` entry (registry.ts:855). This round also keeps `pendingInit` after an offline edit (registry.ts:634), with a test. Leaving the adoption case as a follow-up is reasonable."},{"comment_id":4439290170,"status":"addressed","reply":"Fine as a follow-up. Picking the same folder now returns before the transaction, so that common case no longer drops captures."},{"comment_id":4439290177,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed: the early return happens before `relocateActive` (relocate.ts:43-45), and relocate.test.ts:158-161 checks that the log is empty and the generation stays at 1."},{"comment_id":4439290180,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the removal from 64db30b0."},{"comment_id":4439290186,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed in the context: a rejected relocate shows `relocateUncertain` (workspaces-context.tsx:177-183)."},{"comment_id":4439290193,"status":"addressed","reply":"Not in this round's files. Accepting the reworked test from 64db30b0."},{"comment_id":4439336705,"status":"addressed","reply":"Confirmed: `unchanged: true` goes from relocate.ts:44 through index.ts:349, and the context skips the toast (workspaces-context.tsx:168). Only the first step is tested so far; I opened a separate note about the toast skip."}],"summary":"This round fixes two problems. Picking the folder a workspace already uses no longer shows a misleading toast, and an offline edit no longer clears `pendingInit`. Both work correctly. The one gap is tests: nothing checks that the `unchanged` flag reaches the renderer or that the toast is then skipped. All 14 earlier threads are addressed."}

